<title>SINGAPORE: Indonesia details 3.85 mln bbl May LSWR allocation.</title>
<headline>Indonesia details 3.85 mln bbl May LSWR allocation.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia's state oil company, Pertamina, has announced the loading schedule for its 3.85 million barrels of low sulphur waxy residue (LSWR) for lifting in May, traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>In addition to the allocation, some 500,000 barrels are expected to be rolled over from April, bringing the total to 4.35 million barrels for May, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The May allocation is lower than that in April but demand remains very poor and it's no way prices will recover in the short term,&quot; said one trader.  </p>
<p>    SUB-TOTAL:   1,864</p>
<p>LOADING FROM PAKNING (SUMATRA)</p>
